* - Lines 718-820\nPer-inner-round sequence:\n\n```\nRound 0 (inner):\n  1. GPU: frac_compute_round_and_revert() \n     - Reverts segment tree layer on-the-fly\n     - Computes s'(1), s'(2) for sumcheck polynomial\n     - Output: 2 EF values in d_sum_evals buffer (remains on GPU)\n  \n  2. CPU: observe_and_update() \n     - D2H: Copy d_sum_evals (2 EF) → host\n     - Reconstruct full s(1,2,3) from s'(1,2)\n     - Observe in transcript & sample r[0]\n  \nRounds 1..(round-1) (inner):\n  For each xi_j in xi_prev.skip(1):\n    3. GPU: frac_compute_round_and_fold()  [OUT-OF-PLACE]\n       OR frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace()  [IN-PLACE]\n       - Reads src_pq_buffer at original size\n       - Fuses: compute s'(X) AND fold using r_prev inline\n       - Writes folded output to dst_pq_buffer (size / 2)\n       - Output: 2 EF values in d_sum_evals buffer (GPU)\n    \n    4. CPU: observe_and_update()\n       - D2H: Copy d_sum_evals (2 EF) → host\n       - Reconstruct s(1,2,3)\n       - Observe & sample r[i]\n    \n    5. Repeat for next xi_j with pq_size >>= 1\n\nFinal fold (after last r):\n  6. GPU: fold_ef_frac_columns() or fold_ef_frac_columns_inplace()\n     - Last fold has no compute to fuse (already did compute in round 1..round-1)\n     - Input size pq_size, output size pq_size/2\n```\n\n#### **B. PrecomputeM Strategy** (Optimization path) - Lines 821-1046\n\nFor sufficiently large rounds (rem_n >= min_n, rounds_left >= window_size):\n\n```\nWindow loop (w=3 consecutive rounds fused):\n  For each window in [base..stop):\n    1. GPU: frac_precompute_m_build_raw()\n       - Input: layer buffer at rem_n+1 dimensions (if pending_fold) or rem_n\n       - Builds 2D table: M[eq_low][eq_high] = ∑_y f(eq_r_window, y)\n       - Partial buffers: tiled computation (tail_tile blocks)\n       - Output: m_buffer (2^(2w) EF values), m_partial_buffer\n       - Optionally folds prev_r inline (first iteration only)\n    \n    2. Per-window-element (t in 0..w):\n       GPU: frac_precompute_m_eval_round_raw()\n       - Evaluates M table at specific prefix/suffix eq combinations\n       - Output: d_sum_evals (2 EF values)\n       \n       CPU: observe_and_update()\n       - D2H: d_sum_evals → host\n       - Observe & sample r[base+t]\n    \n    3. GPU: frac_multifold_raw()\n       - Folds w+1 dimensions at once using precomputed eq_r_window\n       - Input: w+1 challenge values (r_fold + window_rs)\n       - Output: folded buffer (size / 2^(w+1))\n\nTail rounds (if base < round):\n  4. GPU: frac_compute_round() + do_fused_sumcheck_round_inplace() loop\n     - Falls back to FoldEval for remaining rounds\n```\n\n### 3. **Synchronization Points (D2H for Challenges)**\n\nCritical blocking points occur at **4 places per inner round**:\n\n```\n// Line 1132 in observe_and_update()\nlet sp_vec = d_sum_evals.to_host()?;  // BLOCKS: Wait for s'(1,2) computation\n\n// Line 334-338 in observe_and_update()\ntranscript.observe_ext(eval);  // CPU: Hash challenge\nlet r = transcript.sample_ext();  // CPU: Sample new r\n\n// Lines 1057-1060 (after all inner rounds per outer round)\nlet pq_host = [\n    copy_from_device(active, 0, &mut copy_scratch)?,      // D2H: Get p(0)\n    copy_from_device(active, pq_size / 2, ...)?  // D2H: Get p(1)\n];\n```\n\n**Per outer round**: ~(round + 1) D2H transfers:\n- Round 0 compute+revert: 1x D2H (2 EF)\n- Rounds 1..(round-1): (round-1)x D2H per inner round (2 EF each)\n- Final layer extraction: 2x D2H (pq_host[0,1])\n- **Total: 2×round + 2 EF values from GPU per outer round**\n\n### 4. **bit_rev_frac_build_k2 and multifold Usage**\n\n**bit_rev_frac_build_k2** (Lines 525-531):\n- Called **once** at initialization (segment tree building)\n- Fuses bitrev + tree layers 0+1 into single kernel (for N > 1024)\n- Eliminates ~1.5N global memory reads\n- Not in the inner GKR loop - only preprocessing\n\n**multifold_kernel** (PrecomputeM path only):\n- Called **per window** (typically 3 rounds per window)\n- Folds w+1 dimensions simultaneously (w=3 → 8D fold)\n- Replaces (w+1) sequential fold calls\n- **Per outer round**: ~(round / GKR_WINDOW_SIZE) multifold calls\n\n### 5. **Data Dependencies Preventing Parallelism**\n\n**Hard dependencies (serial bottlenecks)**:\n\n```\n1. Challenge dependency loop:\n   compute_round() → [D2H] → sample_ext() → compute_next()\n   - Each inner round blocks on previous r\n   - Can't parallelize across inner rounds within same outer round\n\n2. Outer round chaining:\n   final D2H (pq_host) → transcript.observe() → sample mu → \n   SqrtEqLayers::from_xi(new_xi) → next outer round\n   - Each outer round depends on mu from previous round\n\n3. Tree revert ordering:\n   frac_compute_round_and_revert() modifies layer in-place\n   - First layer revert must complete before next compute reads layer\n```\n\n**Soft dependencies (could be hidden by pipelining)**:\n- `eq_buffer.drop_layer()` (line 381, 431, 954): Frees previous eq layer\n- No GPU-side eq layer recomputation (precomputed on CPU)\n- Could potentially pipeline eq_buffer setup → next kernel while current runs\n\n### 6. **Inter-Kernel Gaps Sources**\n\nFrom your profiling (529ms with 486 instances of 472ms evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel):\n\n**Gap analysis**:\n\n```\nTime budget per 529ms LogUp GKR:\n  evaluate_interactions (input eval): 472ms (already multi-streamed)\n  compute_round + revert + fold:      50-70ms\n    - compute_round_and_revert: ~70ms (141 instances @ 0.5ms = 70ms)\n    - fold kernels: ~20-30ms (distributed across multifold/fold calls)\n    - bit_rev_frac_build_k2: ~50ms (6 instances @ 8ms = 48ms)\n  \nRemaining ~7-15ms: D2H transfers + CPU-side work\n  - Per-round D2H (2 EF values): ~10-20μs each\n  - 141 compute_round instances × 20μs = ~2.8ms total D2H time\n  - Transcript observe/sample: ~100μs per round × 141 = ~14ms\n  - CPU eq_buffer setup: ~1-2ms per round × 10 rounds = ~10-20ms\n```\n\n**Gap sources**:\n\n1. **Transcript bottleneck** (10-14ms):\n   - Each inner round: sample r (Fiat-Shamir 