imensions simultaneously (w=3 → 8D fold)\n- Replaces (w+1) sequential fold calls\n- **Per outer round**: ~(round / GKR_WINDOW_SIZE) multifold calls\n\n### 5. **Data Dependencies Preventing Parallelism**\n\n**Hard dependencies (serial bottlenecks)**:\n\n```\n1. Challenge dependency loop:\n   compute_round() → [D2H] → sample_ext() → compute_next()\n   - Each inner round blocks on previous r\n   - Can't parallelize across inner rounds within same outer round\n\n2. Outer round chaining:\n   final D2H (pq_host) → transcript.observe() → sample mu → \n   SqrtEqLayers::from_xi(new_xi) → next outer round\n   - Each outer round depends on mu from previous round\n\n3. Tree revert ordering:\n   frac_compute_round_and_revert() modifies layer in-place\n   - First layer revert must complete before next compute reads layer\n```\n\n**Soft dependencies (could be hidden by pipelining)**:\n- `eq_buffer.drop_layer()` (line 381, 431, 954): Frees previous eq layer\n- No GPU-side eq layer recomputation (precomputed on CPU)\n- Could potentially pipeline eq_buffer setup → next kernel while current runs\n\n### 6. **Inter-Kernel Gaps Sources**\n\nFrom your profiling (529ms with 486 instances of 472ms evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel):\n\n**Gap analysis**:\n\n```\nTime budget per 529ms LogUp GKR:\n  evaluate_interactions (input eval): 472ms (already multi-streamed)\n  compute_round + revert + fold:      50-70ms\n    - compute_round_and_revert: ~70ms (141 instances @ 0.5ms = 70ms)\n    - fold kernels: ~20-30ms (distributed across multifold/fold calls)\n    - bit_rev_frac_build_k2: ~50ms (6 instances @ 8ms = 48ms)\n  \nRemaining ~7-15ms: D2H transfers + CPU-side work\n  - Per-round D2H (2 EF values): ~10-20μs each\n  - 141 compute_round instances × 20μs = ~2.8ms total D2H time\n  - Transcript observe/sample: ~100μs per round × 141 = ~14ms\n  - CPU eq_buffer setup: ~1-2ms per round × 10 rounds = ~10-20ms\n```\n\n**Gap sources**:\n\n1. **Transcript bottleneck** (10-14ms):\n   - Each inner round: sample r (Fiat-Shamir hash)\n   - Sequential: sample blocks until host receives computed values\n   - Cannot parallelize across rounds\n\n2. **eq_buffer CPU construction** (8-10ms):\n   - `SqrtEqLayers::from_xi()` runs on CPU before next round\n   - Evaluates eq(xi, x) hierarchically\n   - Scales with inner round count\n\n3. **Kernel launch overhead**:\n   - 141 kernel launches (compute_round)\n   - ~100-200μs per launch × 141 ≈ 14-28ms\n   - Multi-streamed batching could reduce this\n\n4. **Memory bandwidth saturation**:\n   - compute_round_and_fold reads src_pq (size varies: 2^(2+round) to 2^(round+2) EF)\n   - Writes folded output: size/2\n   - Working set: ~256MB-4GB depending on round\n   - May hit L2 cache misses or memory bandwidth limits\n\n### 7. **Code Paths Summary Table**\n\n| Component | File Path | Lines | GPU/CPU | Instances | Hot Loop? |\n|-----------|-----------|-------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| Main orchestration | fractional.rs | 655-1079 | CPU | 1 | Yes |\n| compute_round_and_revert | logup_zerocheck.rs | 708-739 | GPU | 10 | Yes (first inner round) |\n| frac_compute_round_and_fold | logup_zerocheck.rs | 782-833 | GPU | ~100 | Yes (FoldEval path) |\n| frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace | logup_zerocheck.rs | 843-885 | GPU | ~100 | Yes (FoldEval path) |\n| frac_precompute_m_build_raw | logup_zerocheck.rs | 888-924 | GPU | ~14 | Yes (PrecomputeM path) |\n| frac_precompute_m_eval_round_raw | logup_zerocheck.rs | 925-943 | GPU | ~42 (w=3, 14 windows) | Yes (PrecomputeM) |\n| frac_multifold_raw | logup_zerocheck.rs | 945-955 | GPU | ~14 | Yes (PrecomputeM) |\n| fold_ef_frac_columns* | logup_zerocheck.rs | 744-769 | GPU | ~10 | Yes (final fold) |\n| observe_and_update | fractional.rs | 318-346 | CPU | 141 | Yes (D2H sync) |\n| bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2 | fractional.rs | 525-531 | GPU | 1 | No (init only) |\n\n### Key Findings for Optimization\n\n1. **D2H transfer rate limiting**: Each inner round requires 2 EF (~64 bytes) D2H. At 141 inner rounds total, that's ~9KB per outer round cycle. With PCI-e 4.0 (30 GB/s), this is <1μs but the synchronization point forces serialization.\n\n2. **Transcript hashing bottleneck**: ~14ms of 529ms is Fiat-Shamir challenges. Could be masked if you can parallelize eq_buffer construction or kernel launches while waiting.\n\n3. **PrecomputeM amortizes kernel launches**: Reduces from ~141 to ~70 kernels (42 eval + 14 multifold + 14 build), but still leaves transcript serialization.\n\n4. **No GPU-side parallelism across outer rounds**: Each outer round waits for final mu before starting next."}],"totalDurationMs":68469,"totalTokens":63423,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2443,"cache_read_input_tokens":57415,"output_tokens":3561,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2443},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3561,"cache_read_input_tokens":57415,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2443,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":12,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":9,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
