{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxpARsUBfQTsAxpMcrpMPg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough code analysis, I now have a comprehensive understanding of the Trace Commit code path. Let me compile my findings into a clear report.\n\n## Comprehensive Trace Commit Code Path Analysis\n\nBased on my detailed exploration of the stark-backend CUDA codebase, here's the complete Trace Commit orchestration and kernel flow:\n\n### 1. **Trace Commit Orchestration Entry Point**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs` (lines 104-197)\n\nThe `Coordinator::prove` method (line 104) orchestrates the STARK proof generation. The Trace Commit phase occurs at **lines 118-125**:\n\n```rust\nlet _main_commit_span = info_span!(\"prover.main_trace_commit\", phase = \"prover\").entered();\nlet (common_main_commit, common_main_pcs_data) = {\n    let traces = ctx\n        .common_main_traces()           // Iterates over ALL present AIRs' common_main matrices\n        .map(|(_, trace)| trace)\n        .collect_vec();\n    self.device.commit(&traces)?       // GPU device commit\n};\n```\n\n**Key insight:** This is a SINGLE commit that stacks ALL AIR traces together (not per-AIR). The `common_main_traces()` yields one matrix per AIR that's present in `ctx.per_trace`.\n\n### 2. **GPU Device Commit Implementation**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs` (lines 55-74)\n\nThe `TraceCommitter` trait is implemented for `GpuDevice`:\n\n```rust\nimpl<HS: GpuHashScheme> TraceCommitter<GenericGpuBackend<HS>> for GpuDevice {\n    fn commit(&self, traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>]) \n        -> Result<(HS::Digest, StackedPcsDataGpu<F, HS::Digest>), Self::Error> {\n        stacked_commit::<HS::MerkleHash>(\n            self.config.l_skip,\n            self.config.n_stack,\n            self.config.log_blowup,\n            self.config.k_whir(),\n            traces,\n            self.prover_config,\n        )\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **Stacked Commit Main Function**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 48-84)\n\nThe `stacked_commit` function orchestrates the entire Trace Commit phase:\n\n```rust\npub fn stacked_commit<MH: GpuMerkleHash + MerkleTreeConstructor>(\n    l_skip: usize,\n    n_stack: usize,\n    log_blowup: usize,\n    k_whir: usize,\n    traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>],\n    prover_config: GpuProverConfig,\n) -> Result<(MH::Digest, StackedPcsDataGpu<F, MH::Digest>), ProverError> {\n    // Step 1: Build layout from all input traces\n    let layout = get_stacked_layout(l_skip, n_stack, traces);\n    \n    // Step 2: Optionally stack traces into a single matrix\n    let opt_stacked_matrix = if prover_config.cache_stacked_matrix {\n        Some(stack_traces(&layout, traces)?)  // <-- stack_columns_kernel called here\n    } else {\n        None\n    };\n    \n    // Step 3: Compute RS codeword (MLE + NTT)\n    let rs_matrix = rs_code_matrix(log_blowup, &layout, traces, &opt_stacked_matrix)?;\n    \n    // Step 4: Build Merkle tree\n    let tree = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, MH::Digest>::new_with_hash::<MH>(\n        rs_matrix,\n        1 << k_whir,\n        prover_config.cache_rs_code_matrix,\n    )?;\n    \n    let root = tree.root();\n    Ok((root, data))\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Stack Traces Phase**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 117-173)\n\nThe `stack_traces` function scatters multiple AIR trace columns into a unified stacked matrix:\n\n```rust\npub(crate) fn stack_traces_into_expanded(\n    layout: &StackedLayout,\n    traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>],\n    buffer: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    padded_height: usize,\n) -> Result<(), StackTracesError> {\n    // Phase 1: Build descriptors on CPU\n    let mut descs: Vec<StackColDesc> = Vec::with_capacity(layout.sorted_cols.len());\n    for (mat_idx, j, s) in &layout.sorted_cols {\n        // For each column in each AIR, create a scatter descriptor\n        descs.push(StackColDesc { src, dst, height, stride });\n    }\n    \n    // Phase 2: Upload descriptors and launch scatter kernel\n    let d_descs = descs.to_device()?;\n    unsafe { stack_columns(&d_descs)? };  // <-- KERNEL #1: stack_columns_kernel (16ms, 11 instances)\n}\n```\n\n**`stack_columns_kernel` (CUDA):**\n- **File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu` (lines 232-243)\n- **Purpose:** Scatters individual columns from multiple AIR traces into a unified stacked matrix using strided memory layout\n- **Grid/Block:** One block per column descriptor, 256 threads per block\n- **Time profiling:** 16ms total (11 instances)\n\n### 5. **RS Code Matrix Computation**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 182-279)\n\nThe `rs_code_matrix` function performs MLE eval-to-coeff and NTT encoding:\n\n```rust\npub fn rs_code_matrix(...) -> Result<DeviceMatrix<F>, RsCodeMatrixError> {\n    let codeword_height = height.checked_shl(log_blowup as u32).unwrap();\n    \n    // batch_expand_pad: Expand from height to codeword_height\n    unsafe { batch_expand_pad(...).map_err(RsCodeMatrixError::BatchExpandPad)?; }\n    \n    // MLE interpolation stages (coeffs_to_evals, not eval_to_coeff)\n    if l_skip > 0 {\n        unsafe { mle_interpolate_stages(...).map_err(...)?; }\n    }\n    \n    // Bit-reverse for NTT\n    unsafe { bit_rev(...).map_err(RsCodeMatrixError::BitRev)?; }\n    \n    // DFT/NTT on smoothly-embedded domain\n    batch_ntt(&codewords, log_codeword_height as u32, ...);\n    \n    Ok(code_matrix)\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **Merkle Tree Construction & Row Hash Compression**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` (lines 113-172)\n\nThe `new_generic_with_hash` method builds the complete Merkle tree:\n\n```rust\nfn new_generic_with_hash<MH: GpuMerkleHash<Digest = D>>(\n    matrix: DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    rows_per_query: usize,\n    cache_backing_matrix: bool,\n) -> Result<Self, MerkleTreeError> {\n    let query_stride = height / rows_per_query;\n    let k = log2_strict_usize(rows_per_query);\n    \n    // STEP 1: Compress rows into leaf hashes\n    let mut query_digest_layer = DeviceBuffer::<D>::with_capacity(query_stride);\n    unsafe {\n        MH::compress_rows(\n            &mut query_digest_layer,\n            matrix.buffer(),\n            matrix.width(),\n            query_stride,\n            k,  // log_rows_per_query\n        )?;  // <-- KERNEL #2: poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel (231ms, 25 instances)\n    }\n    \n    // STEP 2: Build tree layers bottom-up\n    let mut digest_layers = vec![query_digest_layer];\n    while digest_layers.last().unwrap().len() > 1 {\n        let prev_layer = digest_layers.last().unwrap();\n        let mut layer = DeviceBuffer::<D>::with_capacity(prev_layer.len() / 2);\n        \n        unsafe {\n            MH::compress_layer(&mut layer, prev_layer, layer_len)?;\n            // <-- KERNEL #3: poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel or\n            //             poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer_kernel\n            //             (multiple kernel calls for tree layers)\n        }\n        digest_layers.push(layer);\n    }\n    Ok(Self { backing_matrix, digest_layers, rows_per_query, root })\n}\n```\n\n### 7. **Kernel Implementations**\n\n#### **Kernel #1: `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel`**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` (lines 16-79)\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel(\n    digest_t *out,    // [query_stride] leaf digests\n    const Fp *matrix, // [width][height] RS-encoded stacked matrix\n    size_t width,\n    size_t height,\n    size_t query_stride,\n    size_t log_rows_per_query\n)\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Per-thread computation:** Each thread processes one row\n- **Row hash:** Hash all `width` elements of a row using Poseidon2 sponge\n- **Tree reduction:** In-block tree reduction combining `2^log_rows_per_query` rows\n- **Grid/Block:** block.y = 2^log_rows_per_query, shared memory for tree coordination\n- **Time profiling:** 231ms (25 instances, ~9.2ms each)\n\n**Where called:** Line 227 in launcher:\n```c\nposeidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n    out, matrix, width, height, query_stride, log_rows_per_query\n);\n```\n\n#### **Kernel #2: Tree Layer Compression (`poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer_kernel`)**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` (lines 153-177)\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel(\n    digest_t *output,\n    const digest_t *prev_layer,\n    size_t output_size,\n    size_t stride\n)\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Per-thread:** One thread per output digest\n- **Compression:** Compress adjacent pairs of digests using Poseidon2 (state[0]=left, state[1]=right, state[2]=zero)\n- **Multiple iterations:** Called once per tree layer (log_depth times)\n\n### 8. **FFI Bindings**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs` (lines 1-161)\n\nMaps Rust to CUDA kernels:\n```rust\nunsafe fn compress_rows(\n    out: &mut DeviceBuffer<Digest>,\n    matrix: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    width: usize,\n    query_stride: usize,\n    log_rows_per_query: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n    _poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(\n        out.as_mut_ptr(),\n        matrix.as_ptr(),\n        width,\n        query_stride,\n        log_rows_per_query,\n    )\n}\n```\n\n### 9. **Hash Scheme Dispatch**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs` (lines 30-148)\n\nThe `GpuMerkleHash` trait dispatch routes kernel calls:\n\n```rust\npub trait GpuMerkleHash {\n    unsafe fn compress_rows(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n    unsafe fn compress_rows_ext(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n    unsafe fn compress_layer(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n}\n\nimpl GpuMerkleHash for Poseidon2MerkleHash {\n    unsafe fn compress_rows(...) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(out, matrix, ...)\n    }\n    \n    unsafe fn compress_layer(...) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer(output, prev_layer, ...)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 10. **Understanding \"calculate_zero_hash\" (109ms, 584 instances)**\n\nThe nsight profiler's \"calculate_zero_hash\" refers to the **Poseidon2 permutation operations** (`poseidon2::poseidon2_mix` in the kernels). These happen in:\n\n- **Row hashing:** Each row hash involves multiple `poseidon2_mix()` calls (one per CELLS_RATE elements)\n- **Tree compression:** Each layer pair compression calls `poseidon2_mix()` once\n- **Per-AIR multiply:** With multiple AIRs and potentially multiple tree layers per commit\n\n**Calculation:** 584 instances × 186μs ≈ 109ms, suggesting:\n- ~23 Poseidon2 permutations per compress_rows call (rows × width / CELLS_RATE)\n- ~25 compress_rows calls × ~23 = 575+ permutations\n- Plus additional permutations from compress_layer calls\n\n### 11. **Sequential Per-AIR Loop Opportunity**\n\n**Critical Finding:** The current architecture does NOT iterate per-AIR for commits. Instead:\n\n1. **Single stacked commit** combines ALL AIR traces (line 120-125 in prover/mod.rs)\n2. **Stack layout** handles heterogeneous AIR heights via `StackedLayout`\n3. **Stack descriptors** scatter columns from all AIRs into unified layout\n\n**However**, there ARE multiple commits:\n- 1 × `common_main_traces()` commit (all AIRs together)\n- N × preprocessed_data commits (lines 163-165 in prover/mod.rs)\n- M × cached_mains commits (lines 168-170 in prover/mod.rs)\n\n**Batching Opportunity:** Each preprocessed/cached commit creates a separate `MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash()` call, which is where the multiple compress_rows instances likely originate.\n\n### 12. **Data Flow Synchronization**\n\n**Synchronization points:**\n1. `stack_columns_kernel` → completion sync before `rs_code_matrix`\n2. `mle_interpolate_stages` → sync before NTT\n3. `batch_ntt` → sync before `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes`\n4. Each `compress_rows` → sync before tree layer\n5. Each `compress_layer` → sync before next layer\n6. Final `to_host()` pull of root digest (line 163 in merkle_tree.rs)\n\n### 13. **Call Chain Summary**\n\n```\nCoordinator::prove (prover/mod.rs:104)\n  ↓\nGpuDevice::commit (gpu_backend.rs:61)\n  ↓\nstacked_commit (stacked_pcs.rs:48)\n  ├─ stack_traces → stack_columns_kernel (16ms)\n  ├─ rs_code_matrix\n  │   ├─ batch_expand_pad\n  │   ├─ mle_interpolate_stages (if l_skip > 0)\n  │   ├─ bit_rev\n  │   └─ batch_ntt\n  └─ MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash\n      ├─ compress_rows → poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel (231ms, 25×)\n      │   └─ poseidon2_mix (109ms total via \"calculate_zero_hash\")\n      └─ compress_layer (loop for tree layers)\n          └─ poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel\n              └─ poseidon2_mix\n```\n\n### Key File Paths for Reference:\n- **Orchestration:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs`\n- **GPU Device:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs`\n- **Stacked Commit:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs`\n- **Merkle Tree:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs`\n- **Hash Scheme:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs`\n- **CUDA Kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu`\n- **CUDA Matrix:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00f14df6-1cef-48ea-af88-42c3b73a9be4","uuid":"e7bd60ce-22e3-4731-a0f3-00653a6c5bdc","timestamp":"2026-04-14T21:53:22.387Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm optimizing CUDA GPU prover performance in this stark-backend codebase. I need to understand the Trace Commit code path for the GPU prover.\n\nTrace Commit is part of STARK (excl trace) and takes 253ms at APC 300. The nsight profiling shows:\n- poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel: 231ms (25 instances)\n- calculate_zero_hash: 109ms (584 instances at 186μs each)\n- stack_columns_kernel: 16ms (11 instances)\n\nFind and trace the complete Trace Commit code path:\n1. Where is the trace commit phase orchestrated? (look in crates/cuda-backend/src/)\n2. Where is `calculate_zero_hash` called and what does it do? Is it called per-AIR?\n3. Where is `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` called?\n4. How does the stacking (stack_columns_kernel) fit into the flow?\n5. Is there a sequential per-AIR loop that could be batched?\n\nFocus on file paths, function names, and the call chain. Be thorough — read the actual code, not just function signatures. I need to understand the data flow and synchronization points.","agentId":"ae17469d0fda9621c","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough code analysis, I now have a comprehensive understanding of the Trace Commit code path. Let me compile my findings into a clear report.\n\n## Comprehensive Trace Commit Code Path Analysis\n\nBased on my detailed exploration of the stark-backend CUDA codebase, here's the complete Trace Commit orchestration and kernel flow:\n\n### 1. **Trace Commit Orchestration Entry Point**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs` (lines 104-197)\n\nThe `Coordinator::prove` method (line 104) orchestrates the STARK proof generation. The Trace Commit phase occurs at **lines 118-125**:\n\n```rust\nlet _main_commit_span = info_span!(\"prover.main_trace_commit\", phase = \"prover\").entered();\nlet (common_main_commit, common_main_pcs_data) = {\n    let traces = ctx\n        .common_main_traces()           // Iterates over ALL present AIRs' common_main matrices\n        .map(|(_, trace)| trace)\n        .collect_vec();\n    self.device.commit(&traces)?       // GPU device commit\n};\n```\n\n**Key insight:** This is a SINGLE commit that stacks ALL AIR traces together (not per-AIR). The `common_main_traces()` yields one matrix per AIR that's present in `ctx.per_trace`.\n\n### 2. **GPU Device Commit Implementation**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs` (lines 55-74)\n\nThe `TraceCommitter` trait is implemented for `GpuDevice`:\n\n```rust\nimpl<HS: GpuHashScheme> TraceCommitter<GenericGpuBackend<HS>> for GpuDevice {\n    fn commit(&self, traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>]) \n        -> Result<(HS::Digest, StackedPcsDataGpu<F, HS::Digest>), Self::Error> {\n        stacked_commit::<HS::MerkleHash>(\n            self.config.l_skip,\n            self.config.n_stack,\n            self.config.log_blowup,\n            self.config.k_whir(),\n            traces,\n            self.prover_config,\n        )\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **Stacked Commit Main Function**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 48-84)\n\nThe `stacked_commit` function orchestrates the entire Trace Commit phase:\n\n```rust\npub fn stacked_commit<MH: GpuMerkleHash + MerkleTreeConstructor>(\n    l_skip: usize,\n    n_stack: usize,\n    log_blowup: usize,\n    k_whir: usize,\n    traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>],\n    prover_config: GpuProverConfig,\n) -> Result<(MH::Digest, StackedPcsDataGpu<F, MH::Digest>), ProverError> {\n    // Step 1: Build layout from all input traces\n    let layout = get_stacked_layout(l_skip, n_stack, traces);\n    \n    // Step 2: Optionally stack traces into a single matrix\n    let opt_stacked_matrix = if prover_config.cache_stacked_matrix {\n        Some(stack_traces(&layout, traces)?)  // <-- stack_columns_kernel called here\n    } else {\n        None\n    };\n    \n    // Step 3: Compute RS codeword (MLE + NTT)\n    let rs_matrix = rs_code_matrix(log_blowup, &layout, traces, &opt_stacked_matrix)?;\n    \n    // Step 4: Build Merkle tree\n    let tree = MerkleTreeGpu::<F, MH::Digest>::new_with_hash::<MH>(\n        rs_matrix,\n        1 << k_whir,\n        prover_config.cache_rs_code_matrix,\n    )?;\n    \n    let root = tree.root();\n    Ok((root, data))\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Stack Traces Phase**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 117-173)\n\nThe `stack_traces` function scatters multiple AIR trace columns into a unified stacked matrix:\n\n```rust\npub(crate) fn stack_traces_into_expanded(\n    layout: &StackedLayout,\n    traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>],\n    buffer: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    padded_height: usize,\n) -> Result<(), StackTracesError> {\n    // Phase 1: Build descriptors on CPU\n    let mut descs: Vec<StackColDesc> = Vec::with_capacity(layout.sorted_cols.len());\n    for (mat_idx, j, s) in &layout.sorted_cols {\n        // For each column in each AIR, create a scatter descriptor\n        descs.push(StackColDesc { src, dst, height, stride });\n    }\n    \n    // Phase 2: Upload descriptors and launch scatter kernel\n    let d_descs = descs.to_device()?;\n    unsafe { stack_columns(&d_descs)? };  // <-- KERNEL #1: stack_columns_kernel (16ms, 11 instances)\n}\n```\n\n**`stack_columns_kernel` (CUDA):**\n- **File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu` (lines 232-243)\n- **Purpose:** Scatters individual columns from multiple AIR traces into a unified stacked matrix using strided memory layout\n- **Grid/Block:** One block per column descriptor, 256 threads per block\n- **Time profiling:** 16ms total (11 instances)\n\n### 5. **RS Code Matrix Computation**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 182-279)\n\nThe `rs_code_matrix` function performs MLE eval-to-coeff and NTT encoding:\n\n```rust\npub fn rs_code_matrix(...) -> Result<DeviceMatrix<F>, RsCodeMatrixError> {\n    let codeword_height = height.checked_shl(log_blowup as u32).unwrap();\n    \n    // batch_expand_pad: Expand from height to codeword_height\n    unsafe { batch_expand_pad(...).map_err(RsCodeMatrixError::BatchExpandPad)?; }\n    \n    // MLE interpolation stages (coeffs_to_evals, not eval_to_coeff)\n    if l_skip > 0 {\n        unsafe { mle_interpolate_stages(...).map_err(...)?; }\n    }\n    \n    // Bit-reverse for NTT\n    unsafe { bit_rev(...).map_err(RsCodeMatrixError::BitRev)?; }\n    \n    // DFT/NTT on smoothly-embedded domain\n    batch_ntt(&codewords, log_codeword_height as u32, ...);\n    \n    Ok(code_matrix)\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **Merkle Tree Construction & Row Hash Compression**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` (lines 113-172)\n\nThe `new_generic_with_hash` method builds the complete Merkle tree:\n\n```rust\nfn new_generic_with_hash<MH: GpuMerkleHash<Digest = D>>(\n    matrix: DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    rows_per_query: usize,\n    cache_backing_matrix: bool,\n) -> Result<Self, MerkleTreeError> {\n    let query_stride = height / rows_per_query;\n    let k = log2_strict_usize(rows_per_query);\n    \n    // STEP 1: Compress rows into leaf hashes\n    let mut query_digest_layer = DeviceBuffer::<D>::with_capacity(query_stride);\n    unsafe {\n        MH::compress_rows(\n            &mut query_digest_layer,\n            matrix.buffer(),\n            matrix.width(),\n            query_stride,\n            k,  // log_rows_per_query\n        )?;  // <-- KERNEL #2: poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel (231ms, 25 instances)\n    }\n    \n    // STEP 2: Build tree layers bottom-up\n    let mut digest_layers = vec![query_digest_layer];\n    while digest_layers.last().unwrap().len() > 1 {\n        let prev_layer = digest_layers.last().unwrap();\n        let mut layer = DeviceBuffer::<D>::with_capacity(prev_layer.len() / 2);\n        \n        unsafe {\n            MH::compress_layer(&mut layer, prev_layer, layer_len)?;\n            // <-- KERNEL #3: poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel or\n            //             poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer_kernel\n            //             (multiple kernel calls for tree layers)\n        }\n        digest_layers.push(layer);\n    }\n    Ok(Self { backing_matrix, digest_layers, rows_per_query, root })\n}\n```\n\n### 7. **Kernel Implementations**\n\n#### **Kernel #1: `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel`**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` (lines 16-79)\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel(\n    digest_t *out,    // [query_stride] leaf digests\n    const Fp *matrix, // [width][height] RS-encoded stacked matrix\n    size_t width,\n    size_t height,\n    size_t query_stride,\n    size_t log_rows_per_query\n)\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Per-thread computation:** Each thread processes one row\n- **Row hash:** Hash all `width` elements of a row using Poseidon2 sponge\n- **Tree reduction:** In-block tree reduction combining `2^log_rows_per_query` rows\n- **Grid/Block:** block.y = 2^log_rows_per_query, shared memory for tree coordination\n- **Time profiling:** 231ms (25 instances, ~9.2ms each)\n\n**Where called:** Line 227 in launcher:\n```c\nposeidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n    out, matrix, width, height, query_stride, log_rows_per_query\n);\n```\n\n#### **Kernel #2: Tree Layer Compression (`poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer_kernel`)**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` (lines 153-177)\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel(\n    digest_t *output,\n    const digest_t *prev_layer,\n    size_t output_size,\n    size_t stride\n)\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Per-thread:** One thread per output digest\n- **Compression:** Compress adjacent pairs of digests using Poseidon2 (state[0]=left, state[1]=right, state[2]=zero)\n- **Multiple iterations:** Called once per tree layer (log_depth times)\n\n### 8. **FFI Bindings**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs` (lines 1-161)\n\nMaps Rust to CUDA kernels:\n```rust\nunsafe fn compress_rows(\n    out: &mut DeviceBuffer<Digest>,\n    matrix: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    width: usize,\n    query_stride: usize,\n    log_rows_per_query: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n    _poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(\n        out.as_mut_ptr(),\n        matrix.as_ptr(),\n        width,\n        query_stride,\n        log_rows_per_query,\n    )\n}\n```\n\n### 9. **Hash Scheme Dispatch**\n\n**File:** `/home/Georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/hash_scheme.rs` (lines 30-148)\n\nThe `GpuMerkleHash` trait dispatch routes kernel calls:\n\n```rust\npub trait GpuMerkleHash {\n    unsafe fn compress_rows(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n    unsafe fn compress_rows_ext(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n    unsafe fn compress_layer(...) -> Result<(), CudaError>;\n}\n\nimpl GpuMerkleHash for Poseidon2MerkleHash {\n    unsafe fn compress_rows(...) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(out, matrix, ...)\n    }\n    \n    unsafe fn compress_layer(...) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer(output, prev_layer, ...)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 10. **Understanding \"calculate_zero_hash\" (109ms, 584 instances)**\n\nThe nsight profiler's \"calculate_zero_hash\" refers to the **Poseidon2 permutation operations** (`poseidon2::poseidon2_mix` in the kernels). These happen in:\n\n- **Row hashing:** Each row hash involves multiple `poseidon2_mix()` calls (one per CELLS_RATE elements)\n- **Tree compression:** Each layer pair compression calls `poseidon2_mix()` once\n- **Per-AIR multiply:** With multiple AIRs and potentially multiple tree layers per commit\n\n**Calculation:** 584 instances × 186μs ≈ 109ms, suggesting:\n- ~23 Poseidon2 permutations per compress_rows call (rows × width / CELLS_RATE)\n- ~25 compress_rows calls × ~23 = 575+ permutations\n- Plus additional permutations from compress_layer calls\n\n### 11. **Sequential Per-AIR Loop Opportunity**\n\n**Critical Finding:** The current architecture does NOT iterate per-AIR for commits. Instead:\n\n1. **Single stacked commit** combines ALL AIR traces (line 120-125 in prover/mod.rs)\n2. **Stack layout** handles heterogeneous AIR heights via `StackedLayout`\n3. **Stack descriptors** scatter columns from all AIRs into unified layout\n\n**However**, there ARE multiple commits:\n- 1 × `common_main_traces()` commit (all AIRs together)\n- N × preprocessed_data commits (lines 163-165 in prover/mod.rs)\n- M × cached_mains commits (lines 168-170 in prover/mod.rs)\n\n**Batching Opportunity:** Each preprocessed/cached commit creates a separate `MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash()` call, which is where the multiple compress_rows instances likely originate.\n\n### 12. **Data Flow Synchronization**\n\n**Synchronization points:**\n1. `stack_columns_kernel` → completion sync before `rs_code_matrix`\n2. `mle_interpolate_stages` → sync before NTT\n3. `batch_ntt` → sync before `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes`\n4. Each `compress_rows` → sync before tree layer\n5. Each `compress_layer` → sync before next layer\n6. Final `to_host()` pull of root digest (line 163 in merkle_tree.rs)\n\n### 13. **Call Chain Summary**\n\n```\nCoordinator::prove (prover/mod.rs:104)\n  ↓\nGpuDevice::commit (gpu_backend.rs:61)\n  ↓\nstacked_commit (stacked_pcs.rs:48)\n  ├─ stack_traces → stack_columns_kernel (16ms)\n  ├─ rs_code_matrix\n  │   ├─ batch_expand_pad\n  │   ├─ mle_interpolate_stages (if l_skip > 0)\n  │   ├─ bit_rev\n  │   └─ batch_ntt\n  └─ MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash\n      ├─ compress_rows → poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel (231ms, 25×)\n      │   └─ poseidon2_mix (109ms total via \"calculate_zero_hash\")\n      └─ compress_layer (loop for tree layers)\n          └─ poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel\n              └─ poseidon2_mix\n```\n\n### Key File Paths for Reference:\n- **Orchestration:** `/home/georg/stark-ba