{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0164xJHUByhd1ao3nNHt3MW8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-0030-drain-gpu-pipeline-before-stark\n2\t\n3\tThe STARK excl trace timing span includes ~150-200ms of GPU pipeline stall at APC 300 caused by async trace generation kernels (especially `apc_apply_bus_kernel`, 609ms GPU time) that are still executing when the STARK prover begins. Per-segment analysis shows segment 0's Trace Commit is 164ms but actual commit work is only ~35ms — the remaining ~130ms is waiting for trace gen GPU kernels to drain. Adding a `current_stream_sync()` before the `stark_prove_excluding_trace` timing span ensures the metric accurately measures STARK work and eliminates GPU resource contention between trace gen and STARK kernels. This disproportionately helps APC 300 (where trace gen launches many more async GPU kernels) vs APC 0 (where trace gen is simpler), directly improving the APC 0/APC 300 scaling ratio.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019zRsp1p4UiKbTrqrDzUkPT","session_id":"00f14df6-1cef-48ea-af88-42c3b73a9be4","uuid":"8f8fd998-632c-4356-94f3-4e0f66082c4c","timestamp":"2026-04-14T22:19:14.061Z"}
