{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RG54XXdZx1Y1LU5gDtuAaH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012YkYxz3VxGyyk32qafn8ji","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-0030-drain-gpu-pipeline-before-stark/plan.md","old_string":"```rust\npub trait ProverDevice<PB: ProverBackend, TS>:\n    TraceCommitter<PB> + MultiRapProver<PB, TS> + OpeningProver<PB, TS>\n{\n    type Error: ...;\n\n    /// Drain any pending device operations from prior phases.\n    /// Called before the STARK timing span to ensure accurate measurement.\n    /// Default implementation is a no-op (for CPU backends).\n    fn drain_pending_device_ops(&self) {}\n}\n```\n\nThis is a backward-compatible change: all existing implementors get the no-op default.","new_string":"```rust\npub trait ProverDevice<PB: ProverBackend, TS>:\n    TraceCommitter<PB> + MultiRapProver<PB, TS> + OpeningProver<PB, TS>\n{\n    type Error: ...;\n\n    /// Drain any pending device operations from prior phases.\n    /// Called before the STARK timing span to ensure accurate measurement.\n    /// Default implementation is a no-op (for CPU backends).\n    fn drain_pending_device_ops(&self) -> Result<(), Self::Error> { Ok(()) }\n}\n```\n\nThis is a backward-compatible change: all existing implementors get the no-op default. The `Result` return type matches the error-handling pattern used throughout the GPU backend (e.g., `ProverError::CurrentStreamSync` variant already exists)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":202139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00f14df6-1cef-48